From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
Date: Sat, 7 Nov 2026 04:14:31 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] soc: apple: sep: xart_guard: encode list entries through
 encode_with

The hand resolution of "let a boot policy change update its xART record"
kept omacom's encode() body (entry_bytes) next to aurora's encode_with(),
which left encode_with() used only by the tests and rustc warning that it
is never used outside them. Encode Linux's list entries through
encode_with(ENTRY_MAGIC, ...) as aurora does. Same bytes: entry_bytes()
is entry_bytes_with(ENTRY_MAGIC, ...), which encode_with() calls.

Signed-off-by: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5.5
---
 drivers/soc/apple/xart_guard.rs | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/soc/apple/xart_guard.rs b/drivers/soc/apple/xart_guard.rs
index e26839c1ab..84d4bfbfeb 100644
--- a/drivers/soc/apple/xart_guard.rs
+++ b/drivers/soc/apple/xart_guard.rs
@@ -344,7 +344,7 @@ fn entry_bytes_with(magic: &[u8; 4], kind: u8, uuid: &[u8; 16]) -> [u8; ENTRY_SI
 
 /// Encodes one list entry.
 pub(crate) fn encode(key: &Key) -> [u8; ENTRY_SIZE] {
-    entry_bytes(key.kind, &key.uuid)
+    encode_with(ENTRY_MAGIC, key)
 }
 
 /// The entry that records this install's first-setup window as consumed.
